mailove (3.8.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The GUI could freeze for 10+ seconds when a dead IMAP connection was
    dropped: KIMAP waits for the connection's socket thread, which hangs
    when a server stops partway through a response. A dropped connection
    now fails its pending work at once and is deleted only after that
    read has timed out, when deleting it no longer waits.
  * Search: the local index answers first, on every account, instead of
    waiting for the server's SEARCH and a re-fetch of its hits. The
    server's answer, where there is one, only adds mail the cache has not
    reached; hits already cached are shown from the cache. One SEARCH is
    sent at a time, and the latest query typed replaces any waiting one.
    A local scan the user has typed past is stopped (sqlite3_interrupt)
    instead of running to the end.
  * Clearing a search refills the folder from the cache on online
    accounts too; the list no longer trickles back through backfill.
  * IMAP: UIDVALIDITY is tracked per mailbox. A quick folder switch could
    compare it against another mailbox's value, discard a sound cache and
    refetch it.
  * More harmless Qt warnings from senders' HTML (zero point sizes,
    "#transparent") are kept out of the log.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Thu, 29 Oct 2026 12:30:00 +0100

mailove (3.8.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * DKIM: a signature with simple header canonicalization (no c= tag,
    e.g. purelymail) was reported invalid on every message held by
    Gmail. Gmail re-folds header lines in its BODY[HEADER] answers,
    which the body fetch had used since 3.0. The message is now fetched
    whole, the header block taken from that, and the re-assembled body
    trusted only when it is the size the server reports; otherwise the
    TEXT section is fetched for it. A failure judged on cached bytes
    refetches the message once before the badge says invalid.
  * IMAP: the unread-count sweep over the account's folders ran on the
    interactive connection, so on a Gmail account with many labels a
    folder click or a refresh of the open folder waited behind it. It
    runs on the background connection now, open folder and INBOX first.
  * Demo mode: names, addresses, subjects and text are painted as fake
    words for screenshots and screen sharing; nothing saves while it is
    on.
  * mailto: links from other apps open the composer in the running
    mailove instead of starting a second one; links that arrive before
    the window or the first account exist are kept until then.
  * OAuth: the sign-in preselects the account's address, and the sign-in
    link can be copied for a browser or profile signed in to a different
    Google or Microsoft account.
  * Replies and forwards carry exactly one "Re: " or "Fwd: ", with the
    localized markers other clients write ("AW:", "SV:", "Odp:", "WG:",
    "TR:", ...) cut first.
  * The signature editor saves after a pause in typing, not only on
    focus loss.
  * The XOAUTH2 SASL plugin's "[SASL-XOAUTH2]" lines no longer reach
    stderr on every login.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Fri, 23 Oct 2026 17:00:00 +0200

mailove (3.7.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A message opened right after switching accounts stays read. The top
    row is opened from the cache before the connection is up, and that
    read mark was sent to the server only if already connected and never
    retried; the next sync then took the server's "unread" and the
    message came back bold on the next visit. Reading a message now
    queues the change like every other flag change: it is sent once the
    connection is up, and the folder is not re-synced over it meanwhile.
  * A header answer that arrives after a local read/unread or forwarded
    mark no longer undoes it. The sync checked for unsent changes when a
    fetch was sent, not when it landed; while a change is still waiting
    to reach the server, what it says now wins.
  * Gmail: reading a message in INBOX also reads its copies under other
    labels ([Gmail]/Important, user labels), so their unread counts no
    longer lag behind until the next check. The same applies to JMAP
    accounts, where one message can sit in several mailboxes. Accounts
    with plain folders (Exchange, Microsoft 365, most IMAP servers) are
    unaffected: there a copy is a separate message.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:15:00 +0200

mailove (3.7.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Meeting invitations show their content. An Outlook/Exchange request
    arrives as empty text and HTML alternatives beside a text/calendar
    part with no name, which read as a blank message with no attachment.
    The invitation is now a card at the top of the body — title, when
    (in local time, Windows zone names understood), where, organizer,
    attendees, description — and is listed as invitation.ics so it can
    be opened in a calendar or saved. The preview line carries the same.
  * A mailto: link clicked in a message opens this client's composer,
    prefilled from the link (to, cc, bcc, subject, body), instead of
    whatever the desktop has registered for mail.
  * Right-clicking a link in a message offers the link's address first.
    A mail address copies as the address alone ("Copy email address"),
    not as the mailto: link with its subject and body.
  * Replying to your own message (from Sent, or your own message in a
    thread) addresses the original recipients rather than yourself, and
    Reply all no longer puts your own address among the recipients.
  * Find in the composer: Ctrl+F opens a find bar over the body —
    as-you-type, F3/Shift+F3 for next/previous, match count, match
    case. The match stays selected when the bar closes.
  * Ending a link in the composer: the link dialog (Ctrl+K or the link
    button) has an "End link" button that puts the caret after the link
    and makes the next thing typed plain — typing at the end of a link
    used to extend it with no way out. The link button lights up while
    the caret is in a link.
  * A reply quoting a signature with a file: image (Outlook for Mac
    writes those) no longer fails to send with "Could not read the
    pasted image": such references point into the sender's disk and are
    dropped from the quote. A pasted image whose scratch file is gone
    is dropped the same way, with a log line, instead of blocking the
    send.
  * A dismissed passphrase prompt during a bulk send now switches
    signing off for the rest of the batch and carries on, instead of
    cancelling the whole send.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Thu, 08 Oct 2026 14:30:00 +0200

mailove (3.7.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Bulk sending, off by default: with compose/bulkSend set in the
    advanced settings a Bulk checkbox appears in the composer. Checked,
    the To field becomes a list (one address per line, or separated by
    commas), Cc/Bcc go away, and Send becomes hold-to-send
    (compose/bulkHoldSecs). Every address gets its own message with its
    own To header and Message-ID, encrypted to that one recipient when
    encryption is on; attachments are carried by each.
  * The batch goes through the Outbox on a connection of its own, so it
    keeps sending while you read mail in another account, at
    compose/bulkDelayMs between messages. A lost connection or an expired
    sign-in pauses it and it reconnects by itself; a rejected address
    fails only that row. Progress (n of total, the address on the wire,
    failures) sits in the top bar with a Cancel that drops what has not
    gone out. Each message's Sent copy is optional (compose/bulkSentCopy).
  * A dismissed passphrase prompt during a bulk send cancels the whole
    send with nothing queued, instead of asking once per recipient and
    sending unsigned.
  * Links in the composer: a typed web or mail address becomes a link
    when the space or line break after it is typed. Ctrl+K (or the link
    button) opens a dialog with the link text and its target as separate
    fields, edits the link under the cursor whole, and can remove it.
  * The advanced settings are readable from QML (Advanced.get), for
    features whose switches live only there.
  * When the GUI thread stalls for more than two seconds a backtrace of
    it is sampled and logged under the "stalled" line (mailove.trace),
    so a freeze can be located rather than only measured.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Wed, 30 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (3.6.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The RPM installed on Fedora and openSUSE but would not start:
    "version `Qt_6_PRIVATE_API' not found". The QML compiler pulled in
    two Qt private symbols whose version those distributions rename per
    Qt release. QML is now compiled to bytecode only; the binary has no
    private Qt imports left (GitHub #5).
  * Gmail set up as a plain IMAP account with the normal Google password
    fails to log in once 2-Step Verification is on, and the server's
    reply was elided to "Application specif..." in the status bar. The
    login error now says what to do (use the Gmail / Google Workspace
    account type, or an app password), and the account sheet says the
    same when the IMAP server is a Gmail one (GitHub #5).
  * A Gmail or Microsoft account signed in with its own or the advanced
    settings' client pair was skipped by every background poll, so its
    unread count never updated while another account was open. The poll
    resolves the client pair the same way the foreground does; a skipped
    account is now logged with the reason.
  * New arrivals in a background account that were spam candidates
    pending their body are remembered per account, so they are still
    filed when that account is opened instead of being forgotten.
  * The AppImage no longer logs "Failed to register with host portal …
    App info not found" on every launch: it announces the desktop entry
    AppImageLauncher wrote if there is one, and none otherwise.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Sat, 27 Sep 2026 12:00:00 +0200

mailove (3.6.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * A reply-all that copies your own address is no longer marked as spam.
    Your server records such mail as an authenticated submission
    (auth=pass) and grades nothing else, which the scorer read as
    "nothing vouches for it" and scored +100. auth=pass now exempts mail
    from your own address; it is never a pass for anyone else's.
    New switch spam/trustAuth in advanced.conf.
  * The "delivered in one hop from a machine with no host name" rule no
    longer fires on your own server's submission line (with ESMTPSA).
  * Without a Public Suffix List (first run before the download lands,
    or offline) the scorer compared full host names, so a shop's link
    reading "packeta.sk" and going to www.packeta.sk scored a mismatch.
    The fallback now errs the other way and can only under-report.
  * A new arrival opened before the prefetch reached it was marked as
    spam by the body rules but left in the inbox; it is filed now, like
    any other arrival. Mail already in the inbox is still never moved.
  * The reading pane occasionally showed the older message one row down
    under a newly arrived one until the folder was reopened: a body
    fetched for a message you had already left was still presented over
    the one you moved to. Such answers are cached and no longer shown,
    and a failed fetch for a message you left no longer blanks the pane.
  * Clicking the status line opens the activity log on that message;
    every status crumb is logged (mailove.status).
  * Copying from the activity log yields a fenced code block, so it
    pastes as a log into a bug tracker or chat rather than as prose.

 -- dusoft <dusoft@staznosti.sk>  Wed, 16 Sep 2026 16:00:00 +0200

